The potential vulnerability is related to improper handling of file uploads, which can lead to a Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application accepts files from users without sufficient validation or restrictions on the file types and contents. In this case, allowing users to upload PDF files without verifying their integrity or ensuring that they do not contain malicious payloads can enable an attacker to upload a crafted PDF that executes arbitrary code on the server when processed. This lack of stringent checks on the uploaded files can compromise the security of the application and the underlying server environment.

